title: Nutanix Prism: Cluster Resilience (API v4)
agents: nutanix
catalog: virtual/nutanix
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check compares the current fault tolerance of the cluster (number of
 node or disk failures the cluster can survive) with the desired fault
 tolerance configured in the cluster. The service goes CRIT if the current
 fault tolerance is lower, e.g. during a rebuild after a node or disk failure.

 The state and an additional minimum fault tolerance can be configured with
 the rule "Nutanix Cluster Resilience". The redundancy factor and the domain
 awareness level are shown as additional information.

 This check requires the Nutanix Prism special agent for API v4 (agent_prism_v4).

discovery:
 One service is created for the cluster.
